Monte-Carlo Simulation Methods
General Approach
Simulate the price of the underlying instrument 

Calculate the payoff at horizon (for a European Option)

Discount the payoff to the present time

Repeat this process n times, storing the results (P1,     P2,…..,  Pn)


Calculate the average payoff.  This is the estimate of the  option price.



