Simulation of Prices
Standard assumption: price P follows a     Geometric Brownian Motion
dP  = mPdt + sPdz
dz = e (dt)0.5
m = expected return (drift)
s = annualized volatility
Implications: prices are to be generated using
P(t+Dt) =P(t) * exp[(m - s2/2) Dt + seDt)]
e is a drawing from the standard normal    distribution
m is zero for futures and forwards and a risk  free rate r for stocks not paying dividends

